-- S-instantiated-reselect (#1909), the REJECT direction -- the ADMISSION
-- tripwire for s-instantiated-reselect-declared.mdk.
--
-- Hand-derived from DICT-SEMANTICS §3 BEFORE running anything.  Same declared
-- structured context, same two ground impls, called at a THIRD type: `nest 'c'`
-- poses `Tag (Wrap Char)`, whose matching set is EMPTY -- `Wrap Char = Wrap Bool`
-- and `Wrap Char = Wrap Int` each have no solution on argument 0 alone.  The goal
-- is GROUND, so the open-world argument (OD2, #1939) does not reach it and it
-- must be REFUTED: REJECT, T-NO-IMPL, on all three verbs.
--
-- 🚨 THE VERDICT IS UNCHANGED ACROSS THIS SLICE BY DESIGN, and saying so is the
-- point.  MEASURED at the pre-slice base `bffced42` on this tree: REJECT with
-- `No impl of Tag for Wrap Char` at 41:16, identically to head.  This row is a
-- TRIPWIRE, not a demonstration -- it cannot go from red to green across the fix
-- and was never expected to.  What it guards is the direction the fix could
-- plausibly have broken: #1909 WIDENS the goal the call site is keyed on, from
-- the slot's bare mono to the predicate's own structured argument, and a widening
-- that admitted the new goal by UNIFYING it against a non-matching impl head
-- would turn this file green.  Green here is the S0.
--
-- ⚠️ VERDICT AND CODE, NO LOCATION: which site owns a refuted structured goal's
-- diagnostic is adjacent to what the neighbouring open-world rows move, so a span
-- assertion would enshrine one arm's answer as the spec.
--
-- ⚠️ TWO `impl Tag` BLOCKS, so Section 4 derives a permutation pair -- correct and
-- wanted: a reject must not depend on declaration order either.
data Wrap a = Wrap a

interface Tag t where
  tagOf : t -> String

impl Tag (Wrap Bool) where
  tagOf _ = "boolW"

impl Tag (Wrap Int) where
  tagOf _ = "intW"

nest : Tag (Wrap a) => a -> String
nest x = tagOf (Wrap x)

main = println (nest 'c')
